7. INTELLIGENT EMPTY STATES

Create a consistent, attractive empty-state system throughout MarketZed.

The application must correctly handle zero listings.

IMPORTANT:

A count of zero means no available listings.

Do not use incorrect negative listing counts or assume that an empty query is an error.

7.1 Homepage conditional sections

Each homepage section must render only when it contains eligible content.

Examples:

- No products: hide product listing sections.
- No rentals: hide rental sections.
- No services: hide services.
- No jobs: hide jobs.
- No swaps: hide swaps.
- No Wanted requests: hide Wanted sections.
- No sponsored listings: hide sponsored listing sections.

Category navigation must always remain accessible.

Do not show empty cards for individual sections.

Do not display large blank areas.

7.2 When every homepage section is empty

If every content section has zero eligible listings, display ONE attractive marketplace-wide empty state.

Do not show a separate empty-state card for every category.

Use an encouraging, friendly message.

Example:

YOUR MARKETPLACE STARTS HERE

Nothing has been listed just yet.

Be the first to share something with Zambia.

Whether you have a product to sell, a property to rent, a service to offer or a skill to share, MarketZed is ready for you.

[Post Your First Listing]

The message should feel welcoming, not technical.

7.3 Random encouraging messages

Support a collection of approved encouraging messages.

