8. WANTED POSTING — ONE FREE POST, THEN ACCOUNT VERIFICATION

Introduce a controlled Wanted posting entitlement system.

Every eligible account receives ONE free Wanted request.

After the first free Wanted request has been used, the user must complete account verification before publishing additional Wanted requests.

Example verification fee:

K30

This is a proposed one-time account verification fee, subject to the actual approved payment configuration.

8.1 First Wanted post

When a user attempts to publish their first Wanted request:

- Check the account's free Wanted entitlement.
- Allow one free publication.
- Do not require payment for the first eligible post.
- Record that the free entitlement has been consumed only after successful publication.
- Show a clear confirmation.
- Publish the Wanted request normally.

Example:

Your first Wanted post is FREE!

Share what you are looking for and let sellers find you.

[Continue]

8.2 After the free Wanted post

When the user attempts another Wanted publication:

Check the account's verified status.

If not verified, show an attractive verification screen.

Example:

UNLOCK MORE WANTED POSTS

You've used your free Wanted post.

Verify your account to continue publishing additional Wanted requests.

K30

One-time account verification

[Verify Account]

Do not charge per Wanted post.

Verification is an account-level entitlement, not a separate fee for every additional Wanted listing.

8.3 Verified users

Once verification has been successfully confirmed:

- Allow additional Wanted posts.
- Do not charge again for the same verification entitlement.
- Preserve verification status across sessions.
- Allow normal Wanted listing management.
- Apply standard listing moderation and publishing rules.

8.4 Entitlement tracking

Maintain trusted account-level fields or an equivalent secure entitlement model.

Conceptual fields:

- freeWantedPostUsed.
- verified.
- verificationStatus.
- verificationPaymentId.
- verificationDate.

Adapt to the existing Firestore schema rather than blindly introducing incompatible fields.

The entitlement must be enforced by trusted backend logic and Firestore Security Rules.

Do not rely only on a hidden or disabled button.

Prevent:

- Multiple free posts through concurrent requests.
- Free entitlement reuse after logout.
- Free entitlement reuse after reinstalling.
- Duplicate verification charges.
- Unauthorized verification.
- Publishing additional posts before required verification.

If a free Wanted publication fails, do not consume the free entitlement.

8.5 Verification visibility

Make verification accessible from:

- Account profile.
- Wanted posting flow.
- Payment screens.
- Relevant notifications.

Use consistent wording and pricing across the application.

